# Change Control & Git Workflow

## Branches

- `main` — protected, tagged releases only. Never commit or push to it directly.
- `develop` — integration branch; everything merges here first.
- `feature/<name>`, `fix/<name>`, `chore/<name>` — off `develop`.

## Commits (Conventional Commits)

`<type>(<scope>): <short description>`, with an optional body explaining why.

- **Types:** `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `test`, `chore`
- **Scopes:** `api`, `extractor`, `report`, `cli`, `config`, `tests`, `docs`, `port-mapping`, `web`, `ui`, `packaging`

## Before a commit

The `quality-gate` skill (or CI) must be green, no secrets are staged, and `CHANGELOG.md` (or the item's changelog fragment) covers user-facing changes. Versioning is semantic (MAJOR breaking CLI/config, MINOR features, PATCH fixes); the release procedure is in `release-packaging-12` and the `prepare-release` / `ship-release` skills.
